# THE VENDORED TYPEFACES ARE BINARY AND MUST NEVER BE LINE-ENDING FILTERED.
#
# Git normally detects binary content on its own, and on these files it does.
# The rule is here anyway because the cost of being wrong is asymmetric: this
# machine checks out with autocrlf=true, tests/test_font_assets.cpp compares
# the compiled-in bytes against these files byte for byte, and a single
# translated 0x0a inside a TrueType table produces a font that fails to
# rasterise on someone else's clone with nothing in the diff to show it.
#
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.lib binary

# THE TRANSLATION CATALOGUES ARE LF ON EVERY CHECKOUT, for the same reason.
# tools/embed-lang.py compiles their exact bytes into core/lang_assets.hpp and
# test_i18n checks the two agree; with autocrlf=true a plain checkout would
# turn every line ending into CRLF on disk, and a fresh Windows clone would
# fail that check while the Linux build passed it.
resources/lang/*.json text eol=lf

# THE VENDORED ENGINE API HEADER IS BYTE-FOR-BYTE THE UPSTREAM FILE: its
# SHA-256 is recorded in third_party/THIRD_PARTY.md and third_party/
# foxsdr_api/README.md, and a CRLF checkout would make that record false.
third_party/foxsdr_api/foxsdr_api.h text eol=lf

# Everything else in the tree keeps git's default handling.
